id: tz_non_secure_execution
label: TrustZone Non-Secure Execution
description: >
  This Non-Secure execution component is designed to be the default
  choice for any applications that do not implement a full TrustZone solution.  It ensures compatibility with prebuilt libraries, such as Rail,  and facilitates seamless integration.

  The component transitions the application's execution mode to
  Non-Secure, managing both Secure and Non-Secure environments.  The Secure portion is limited to startup operations, where  the core, peripherals, and memory are configured for Non-Secure  execution. Once transitioned, the application runs entirely in  the Non-Secure environment, only returning to the Secure world in  the event of a Secure Fault.

  Note: This component is designed specifically for TrustZone-unaware
  applications. It is not intended as a template or framework for
  building Secure or Non-Secure applications. For those use cases,  refer to the `trustzone_secure` and `trustzone_nonsecure` components.
package: platform_core
category: Platform|TrustZone
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
root_path: platform_core/platform/common
source:
- path: src/sl_tz_non_secure_execution.c
define:
- name: SL_TZ_NON_SECURE_EXECUTION
- name: configRUN_FREERTOS_SECURE_ONLY
  value: 0
- name: configENABLE_TRUSTZONE
  value: 0
provides:
- name: tz_non_secure_execution
- name: tz_execution
requires:
- name: device_series_3
- name: trustzone_unaware
- name: sl_common
conflicts:
- name: ram_only_execution
template_contribution:
- name: tz_non_secure_execution
  value: 1
